{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And YHWH went before them by day.</b> We know that HaShem dwells forever and holy is His name (Isaiah 57:15), and He sat from eternity, Selah (Psalms 55:20). And the verse speaks in the language of human beings, because the power of HaShem went with Israel like one who leads at the right hand of Moses, the arm of His glory (Isaiah 63:12)." "And the meaning of \"in a pillar of cloud\" is that it was not like the form of clouds, but like the form of a pillar extending from the heavens upon the earth. And it was called a pillar because the structure of a house stands upon it." "And the meaning of \"to go by day and night\" is that the camp was large, and they could not travel more than a short journey. Therefore they would travel part of the day and also part of the night. And these two pillars were before them until they came to the sea, as I shall explain."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:15.760255939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}